## Environment Variables

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/multi-target-environment.rules.mdc`

Starter env template:

- `.env.example` — provider-agnostic placeholders only; safe to commit
- `.env` — local values only; never commit

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` locally and fill placeholders when needed.

### Simple starter env model

Single-application projects may use:

```text
UI_BASE_URL = UI application base URL for ui-chromium and e2e projects

API_BASE_URL = API project/tests base URL

UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL = optional API backend for UI/E2E precondition setup

UI_API_BASE_URL = optional documented fallback for UI precondition API base
```

Rules:

- API tests use `API_BASE_URL`;
- UI and E2E browser tests use `UI_BASE_URL`;
- UI API precondition setup must use an API backend aligned with the UI runtime backend when preconditions are implemented;
- specs must not read environment variables directly;
- specs must not derive API host from UI host;
- config/env access belongs in approved config or fixture layer.

Do not hardcode product URLs in the starter. Set values in local `.env` or CI secrets for each concrete project.

Example shape only (placeholders — not real URLs):

```text
UI_BASE_URL=https://your-ui-host.example
API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example
UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example
```

### Multi-target env model

Real projects with multiple UI applications, microfrontends, or API/microservices must extend env ownership here before use.

This project map is the **source of truth** for app and service env names.

Examples only — register actual names per concrete project:

```text
CUSTOMER_UI_BASE_URL = customer-facing UI app
ADMIN_UI_BASE_URL = admin UI app
CHECKOUT_UI_BASE_URL = checkout UI app or microfrontend

AUTH_API_BASE_URL = authentication service
CATALOG_API_BASE_URL = catalog service
ORDER_API_BASE_URL = order service
PAYMENT_API_BASE_URL = payment service
```

Multi-target rules:

- agents must not invent env variable names;
- feature plans must identify target UI app(s), API service(s), and precondition service(s) when more than one exists;
- E2E journey plans must document every UI app and service crossed;
- do not use generic `API_BASE_URL` when the feature belongs to a specific service;
- do not use generic `UI_BASE_URL` when the feature belongs to a specific UI app;
- update `.env.example` with commented examples that match registered names;
- if target ownership is unclear, mark blocked/postponed or request clarification before implementation.

