## API

Environment variables:

- `API_BASE_URL` — API project/tests base URL;
- `UI_PRECONDITION_API_BASE_URL` — optional API backend for UI/E2E precondition setup when documented;
- `UI_API_BASE_URL` — optional fallback for UI precondition API base.

API documentation / contract source:

- define in project-specific feature plans at `specs/<feature>.md`;
- do not hardcode product API URLs in the starter.

API specs (when added):

- `tests/api/**/*.api.spec.ts`

API Playwright project:

- `api`

Shared schema assertion helper (created per project when API schema validation is implemented):

- `src/test/assertions/api/zod-schema.assertion.ts`

API clients (when added):

- `src/test/api/clients/`

API schemas (when added):

- `src/test/schemas/api/`

API types (when added):

- `src/test/api/types/`

UI precondition setup (when added for a concrete project):

- implement in approved project fixture layers;
- UI specs must not read environment variables directly;
- UI specs must not derive API host from UI host;
- setup must verify only required precondition creation and must not hide the UI action under test.

Rules:

- API tests must use the documented API contract as source of truth;
- API tests must not guess payload fields, status codes, or response fields;
- if the API contract is unclear or incomplete, stop and report missing information;
- API tests use request/response model;
- API tests must not use Page Objects or Component Objects;
- API clients are thin and optional;
- API clients must not contain assertions or Allure usage;
- API specs may use the shared Allure metadata helper.

