## Cross-Browser And Responsive Testing

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/browser-and-responsive-testing.rules.mdc`

Default policy:

- broad browser/device matrix is **not** the default;
- do not run every UI or E2E test in every browser or viewport by default;
- API and schema tests are browser-independent and must not be duplicated per browser;
- cross-browser and responsive coverage are focused additions for documented browser or viewport risks only.

Current Playwright browser projects (`playwright.config.ts`):

- `ui-chromium` — focused UI specs (`*.ui.spec.ts`); Desktop Chrome; default viewport `1280x720`
- `api` — API specs; no browser
- `e2e` — E2E specs (`*.e2e.spec.ts`); uses default browser/viewport from shared `use` config unless a project override is added later

Not configured yet:

- dedicated Firefox or WebKit UI projects;
- dedicated mobile/tablet viewport projects;
- dedicated cross-browser or responsive CI jobs

Tag policy:

- see Tag Registry for registered tags and forbidden browser/device tag names;
- use `@cross-browser` or `@responsive` only when explicitly planned;
- browser and viewport details belong to Playwright project configuration and Allure reporting metadata.

Planning:

- feature plans may include Cross-browser coverage, Responsive coverage, or an explicit note that no extra coverage is needed;
- E2E cross-browser expansion belongs in `specs/e2e/<journey>.md`, not feature coverage plans;
- do not invent browser, device, or unregistered coverage-type tags.

Skills:

- planning: `.cursor/skills/plan-test-coverage/SKILL.md`
- UI implementation: `.cursor/skills/implement-ui-feature/SKILL.md`
- review: `.cursor/skills/review-generated-code-quality/SKILL.md`

