## E2E Testing

Rule:

- `.cursor/rules/e2e-testing.rules.mdc`

Intended E2E spec location:

- `tests/e2e/**/*.e2e.spec.ts`
- no E2E specs implemented yet
- create only the minimal directory path needed when the first approved E2E spec is implemented

E2E journey plan location:

- `specs/e2e/<journey>.md`
- E2E is **not** part of feature coverage plans at `specs/<feature>.md`

Planning separation:

- `specs/<feature>.md` = API, UI, schema, visual, not automated coverage
- `specs/e2e/<journey>.md` = full user/business journey plans only

E2E journey plan content must include:

- business value;
- user journey steps;
- setup strategy;
- data strategy;
- cleanup or isolation strategy;
- final outcome/assertion;
- why API/UI/schema coverage is not sufficient;
- flakiness risks;
- blocked or postponed reason when setup, cleanup, or external dependencies are unsafe.

Implementation policy:

- implement only E2E coverage marked ready to implement now in the E2E journey plan;
- do not implement blocked or postponed E2E scenarios;
- do not create E2E scenarios from scratch during implementation;
- do not convert short UI functional tests into E2E;
- E2E journey plans may reuse API/UI capabilities but must not duplicate their coverage.

Layer tag:

- `@e2e` (see Tag Registry)

Required execution-scope tags:

- `@smoke` or `@regression` (see Tag Registry; every E2E test must also have one of these)

Layer tag policy:

- `@e2e` replaces `@ui` as the layer tag for full-journey E2E specs by default;
- focused UI functional tests keep `@ui`;
- browser-based E2E may run in existing browser projects but must be tagged `@e2e` for reporting and filtering.

What E2E covers:

- full user or business flows crossing multiple states, pages, or system boundaries;
- not short page, form, control, or validation-only UI tests.

Planning requirements for E2E scenarios:

- documented in `specs/e2e/<journey>.md`, not in feature coverage plans;
- business value;
- user journey;
- systems or states crossed;
- setup strategy;
- test data strategy;
- cleanup or isolation strategy;
- final assertion;
- why API/UI/schema coverage is not sufficient;
- flakiness risks;
- blocked or postponed reason when setup, cleanup, or external dependencies are unsafe.

Planning skill for feature coverage:

- `.cursor/skills/plan-test-coverage/SKILL.md` (does not include E2E)

E2E journey planning:

- skill: `.cursor/skills/plan-e2e-journey/SKILL.md`
- command: `.cursor/commands/plan-e2e-journey.md`
- output: `specs/e2e/<journey>.md`

Implementation skill:

- `.cursor/skills/implement-e2e-flow/SKILL.md`

Implementation command:

- `.cursor/commands/implement-e2e-flow.md`

Playwright project status:

- dedicated Playwright `e2e` project is configured in `playwright.config.ts`;
- E2E project targets `tests/e2e/**/*.e2e.spec.ts`;
- E2E project retains trace/screenshots/videos on failure;
- E2E retries are CI-aware (`CI ? 1 : 0`);
- if no runner matches the intended E2E spec path or pattern, stop and report the config gap.

User-facing workflow docs:

- `docs/reference/AI_WORKFLOW_MAP.md`
- `docs/reference/HOW_TO_USE_AI_AUTOMATION.md`
- `docs/reference/AI_AGENT_PROMPTS.md`
